 ## What It Is
 
 A clip capturing a single, actionable piece of advice or insight that the audience can apply immediately. The value is dense and specific.
 
-## Why It Works
+## Why Test This Pattern
 
-Practitioners share tactics. When someone hears a specific, usable insight, they save it, screenshot it, or send it to a colleague. Treat saves and bookmarks as outcomes to measure, not a guaranteed advantage over other clip styles.
+The intended response is that a viewer finds the advice useful enough to save or share. Whether that happens must be measured. Compare saves, bookmarks, and shares with comparable clips; this review does not establish an advantage over other clip styles.
 
 ## Selection Criteria
 
 - One clear, actionable insight
 - Advice is specific enough to act on immediately
 - No jargon that requires context to understand
-- Works for both beginners and experienced practitioners
+- Fits the intended audience’s knowledge level; do not assume the same advice serves beginners and experienced practitioners equally
 
 ## When Not To Use
 
 Avoid when the advice requires significant context to understand, or when the insight is too basic for the target audience.
 
 
